article en "Direct-foreign syntax archive v1"
body
  cons paragraph
    cons sentence
      cons text "The opt-in "
      cons code "nepl3.syntax-archive"
      cons text " revision 1 root "
      cons code "SyntaxArchive"
      cons text " has a "
      cons code "sources"
      cons text " field of "
      cons code "nepl3.source-archive"
      cons text " revision 1 "
      cons code "SourceSets"
      cons text " and a "
      cons code "skeleton: Bytes"
      cons text " field."
      nil
    cons " Its separate schema leaves the exact SourceSets descriptor identity unchanged."
    cons " Both interface contracts are checked against Rust descriptors and registered together with foundation revision 1 before boundary use."
    nil
  cons paragraph
    cons "Skeleton bytes encode a structurally checked foundation SyntaxBundle with empty source lists in the root bundle and every directly traversed ForeignSyntax bundle."
    cons " They are not advertised as a semantically valid standalone syntax value."
    cons " Each bundle consumes one explicit source set in deterministic child-first Finish order."
    cons " Its source declarations are restored before node/origin/span/source-map resolution."
    cons " Nonempty skeleton declaration lists, missing sets and extra sets are rejected."
    cons " An empty membership set grants no declarations, including when other sets or the admission ledger contain matching sources."
    nil
  cons paragraph
    cons "Encoding validates the original native graph."
    cons " Decoding validates the outer archive schema, the source-set boundary and the skeleton's structural schema; then reconstructs through the shared typed bundle decoder."
    cons " Existing canonical node/reachability checks remain, and final native validate_with_sources is required before publication."
    cons " Budget and admission are shared across all steps."
    nil
  cons paragraph
    cons "Opaque token payloads remain unchanged, even if they contain nested source text."
    cons " This stage covers direct ForeignSyntax fields only; complete typed token/view ownership adapters are unfinished."
    cons " It is not enabled on default Doc conversion."
    cons " Existing v1 semantic identity uses the reconstructed native value and legacy expanded encoding."
    cons " Neither skeleton bytes nor archive bytes may replace it."
    nil
  cons section descriptor "Replaced-field descriptor boundary"
  body
    cons paragraph
      cons "Empty skeleton source lists do not establish their element types."
      cons sentence
        cons text " Before encode or decode, SyntaxArchive requires the selected Foundation descriptor to declare SyntaxBundle field 0 as "
        cons code "sources: List(SourceContent)"
        cons text "."
        nil
      cons " GroupArchive also requires ForeignProvenance field 1 to have that exact contract."
      cons sentence
        cons text " Each SourceContent named reference uses package "
        cons code "nepl3.foundation"
        cons text ", revision 1."
        nil
      cons " These checks apply even to empty inputs; an archive deliberately requires its complete replacement contract."
      cons " The selected SchemaRef must match the finalized registry."
      cons " Descriptor lookups and comparisons are charged to the current Budget and respect sticky cancellation."
      cons " These checks supplement full original-native validation, checked skeleton and source-table boundaries, and reconstructed-native validation; they do not change v1 descriptors, wire bytes, or component identities."
      nil
    nil
  nil
